{
  "requirement": "`habeas setup` MUST find an ancestor containing both `Cargo.toml` and `book.toml`, require a nonempty relative mdBook source path without parent components and a `SUMMARY.md` at that path, and report an error when these prerequisites are absent or invalid.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "The implementation covers the requirement's obligations, but the tests miss the root-discovery obligations, and one function that duplicates the validation is marked only {cite}.\n\n**Implementation, which looks correct**\n- `find_project_root` (src/setup.rs:56-64) walks `cwd.ancestors()` for a directory with both `Cargo.toml` and `book.toml`.\n- `project_root` (src/setup.rs:66-71) reports \"cannot find a project with Cargo.toml and book.toml\" when none is found.\n- `book_source` (src/setup.rs:35-46) defaults to `src` when `[book]` or `src` is absent. It errors if `book` is not a table or `book.src` is not a string.\n- `run` (src/setup.rs:92-189) rejects an empty source and any path with components other than Normal or CurDir. That excludes parent, root and prefix components. It then requires `SUMMARY.md` in the source directory and errors if it is missing.\n\n**Gaps**\n1. **Cite-only code.** `is_configured` (src/setup.rs:191-265) repeats the source-path checks: empty source, component filter and `SUMMARY.md` existence. It carries only `{cite}` for `requirements.cli.setup_project`. The assessment rules call code that implements part of the requirement under a cite-only reference a gap.\n2. **Untested root discovery.**\n   - No test runs `habeas setup` from a directory that has no `Cargo.toml` and `book.toml` ancestor. The only \"cannot find a project\" assertion is in tests/commands.rs, for `status`, and it carries no `{test}` reference to this requirement.\n   - No test runs `setup` from a nested directory.\n   - No test has only one of the two files present, which is the \"both files\" part of the requirement.\n3. **Narrow test inputs.** The rejection test (tests/setup.rs:188-241) checks `''`, `/outside` and `../outside`. It does not check an embedded parent component such as `a/../b`. It also does not check that a `./` path is accepted.\n\n**What is covered**\n- tests/setup.rs:165-186 covers the default `src` source and the non-string `book.src` case, though the non-string error is asserted only through `session_start`.\n- tests/setup.rs:188-241 covers a non-table `book`, a non-string `src`, empty, absolute and `..` sources, and a missing `SUMMARY.md`.\n\nNo FIXME comments acknowledge these gaps.",
